# Performance Check on New Features

Bastion Bomber ships as a no-threads web export. Frame-time and bake regressions show up as jank or freezes in the browser, so performance is part of feature work — not a later cleanup step.

**After implementing or changing a feature with runtime impact, run the perf gate before calling the work done:**

```bash
tools/perf_check.sh
```

Follow `.cursor/skills/perf-check/SKILL.md` for budgets, interpretation, CI vs local, and what the gate does not measure (real mobile browsers).

## Required when the change touches

- Shaders, materials, post-FX, particles, or draw-heavy visuals
- Island generation, baking, scenic placement, or level activation
- Scene structure, node counts, spawn density, combat/effects load
- Main-loop / `_process` / `_physics_process` work, UI overlays that tick every frame

## Skip only when

- Pure docs, copy, comments, or skill/rule text with no runtime effect
- Version-bump-only commits

## How to treat results

1. **Local FAIL** → fix the regression (or get an explicit user-approved budget tradeoff). Do not ship a silent budget raise.
2. **CI FAIL on llvmpipe** → usually recalibrate `PERF_SCALE` in `.github/workflows/perf-check.yml` from the artifact; do not treat software-GL timings as iPhone/browser proof.
3. Report the gate outcome (pass/fail + notable gates) when finishing feature work.
